# Documentation Maintenance

When editing NestFlow docs:

- Follow `docs/engineering/DOCS_STYLE.md` (Apple Style Guide + DocC page shape).
- Lead with a one-sentence abstract. Use second person, present tense, and active voice.
- Put how-to steps in numbered, imperative lists. Don't use *please*, *simply*, or *just*.
- Update `docs/CHANGELOG.md` only for released, user-visible changes (use `[Unreleased]` until tagged).
- Record significant technical choices as ADRs in `docs/decisions/`.
- Record significant UX or visual choices in `docs/design/DESIGN_DECISIONS.md`.
- Keep `docs/memory/OBSIDIAN_MEMORY.md` in sync with approved decisions only.
- Never store secrets, API keys, passwords, or personal employee data in docs.
- Prefer precise language. Follow the dash-usage project rule.
- Cross-link related docs instead of duplicating long explanations.
- Mark unfinished work as not shipped or ops pending. Don't describe a plan as live behaviour.
